      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nDocument the aggregation semantics of NIXL KV connector transfer metrics so users correctly interpret the CLI log line in multi-rank (TP > 1) deployments.\r\n\r\nFixes #41230\r\n\r\nStats from each TP rank are concatenated before summary statistics (avg, P90, throughput) are computed. This was not clearly documented and has caused confusion — e.g. treating \"Throughput (MB/s)\" as aggregate system throughput or \"Num successful transfers\" as per-engine.\r\n\r\nChanges:\r\n- Module-level docstring in `vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/nixl/stats.py` explaining the rank-aggregation model and the meaning of each logged field\r\n- Improved `aggregate()` and `reduce()` docstrings with explicit multi-rank semantics\r\n- Documented the `observe → aggregate → reduce → log` pipeline in `metrics.py`\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nDocumentation-only change. No runtime behavior modified.\r\n\r\n- Review the new docstrings for accuracy against the existing `aggregate()` / `reduce()` implementation\r\n- Confirm no functional code paths were altered\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\nN/A (docs only). Diff is limited to comments and docstrings in:\r\n- `vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/nixl/stats.py`\r\n- `vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/metrics.py`",
